       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled outpatient and inpatient dose of ibuprofen, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory or rheumatologic conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), which is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first. I can then enter it with a note recording that."
      }
